# ==============================================================
# AI Agent Workflows — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for `vercel dev`, and set the same
# two values in the Vercel dashboard for Production and Preview.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .gitignore already excludes .env and .env.local. This example
# file is the only one that should ever be committed.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vercel only picks up a changed environment variable on
# the NEXT deployment. Set it, then redeploy, or the functions keep
# reporting not_configured.
# ==============================================================


# --------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Secrets. Server side only. These are read by the functions in
#    /api and never reach the browser.
# --------------------------------------------------------------

# Cloudflare Turnstile secret key, from the same page as your site key.
# Read by /api/verify-turnstile.
# Cloudflare's test keys, for forcing a result during development:
#   1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA  always passes
#   2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA  always fails
# A test secret only accepts the dummy token a test site key issues, so
# the pair has to be swapped together.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# The Make Scenario 2 webhook URL, complete.
# Read by /api/approve, which forwards approval decisions to it.
# This used to sit in approve.js where anyone could read it off the page
# and post to it directly. It belongs here instead.
MAKE_APPROVAL_WEBHOOK_URL=


# ==============================================================
# 2. NOT in this file, and not in this repository at all.
#
# These never touch the website. They live inside Make, in the
# connection settings of the relevant module.
#
#   Make webhook token        the secret on the Scenario 1 webhook URL,
#                             also typed into the Scenario 1 filter.
#                             The most important one: whoever has it can
#                             create Airtable records and spend your
#                             agent credits.
#   Airtable access token     the Airtable connection in both scenarios.
#   Firecrawl API key         the Firecrawl app or the HTTP module.
#   Gmail account             connected through OAuth, no key to store.
#
# If any of these leaks, rotate it at the source. Nothing in this
# repository needs changing.
# ==============================================================


# ==============================================================
# 3. Public by design. Do NOT move these here.
#
# This site has no build step, so there is nothing to substitute a
# variable into a static file. More importantly, these values are
# ones the browser must have in order to work, which means they are
# readable by anyone who views source no matter where you put them.
# Hiding them in an env file would only make them harder for you to
# find while leaving them exactly as public.
#
#   YOUR_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY   index.html. Cloudflare intends this to
#                             be public; the secret key above is the
#                             half that matters.
#   YOUR_JOTFORM_FORM_ID      index.html. The iframe URL shows it.
#   YOUR_VERCEL_DOMAIN        index.html, in the canonical and Open
#                             Graph tags. These have to be literal
#                             text in the HTML for crawlers to read.
#   YOUR_BOOKING_LINK         A public booking page.
#   YOUR_PORTFOLIO_URL        Public links in the footer.
#   YOUR_GITHUB_URL
#   YOUR_CONTACT_EMAIL
#   YOUR_DEMO_VIDEO_URL
#
# The approval webhook URL used to belong in this list. It does not
# any more, because /api/approve means the browser never needs it.
# ==============================================================
